# Downloaded AI model weights. They live on the PC, never in git.
#
# The nightly Daily Seal commits whatever is in the folder, and on 26 October that swept in the
# FLUX.1-schnell weights: 8.7 GB, including one 6.4 GB and one 2.6 GB file. GitHub refuses any Git
# LFS object over 2 GB, so from that night onward EVERY push from this repo failed - the seal of the
# 26th, the seal of the 27th, and anything built on top of them. Two nights of company memory sat on
# one laptop instead of reaching GitHub, and nothing said so out loud.
#
# The weights are a reproducible download (Hugging Face), not company memory. They stay on disk and
# out of history.
Tools/openvino-models/

# Model weights anywhere else, by extension, so the next download does not repeat this.
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.gguf

# Installed packages. They are a reproducible `npm install`, not company memory.
#
# Same story as the weights above, second time. On 28 October the Daily Seal swept in
# `Lounge Desktop/node_modules` - 60,972 files - because `Lounge Desktop/package.json` listed itself
# as a dependency ("coco-lounge-desktop": "file:"), so npm copied the package into its own
# node_modules, and that copy into its own, about sixty levels deep, each level carrying another
# 180 MB electron.exe. GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB, so every push from this repo failed from
# that night on and nine commits sat on one laptop. The self-dependency is gone and nothing imports
# it by name; this line is so that a reinstall can never post it back.
node_modules/
